Scenario: View new dxp project
	@ help.center.acceptance = "true"
	@ help.center.smoke = "true"
	New DXP projects that are added to Zendesk via OSB sync should have the appropriate parameters and tags.

	Given I generate a provisioning project name
	And I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code     | OSBZENOSBZEN                  | |
	| Language | English                       | |
	| Name     | Osbzen - ${staticProjectName} | |
	| Region   | United States                 | |
	| Status   | Active                        | |
	| Tier     | T1                            | |
	And I create a postal address for an account with the name "Osbzen - ${staticProjectName}" on koroneiki with the following values
	| Country               | United States   |
	| Locality              | Diamond Bar     |
	| Region                | California      |
	| Type                  | Business        |
	| Mailing               | True            |
	| Postal Code           | 91765           |
	| Primary               | True            |
	| Street Address Line 1 | 123 Main Street |
	And I generate static start and end dates
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Osbzen - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "DXP Production" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         |   |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} |   |
	| Perpetual               | false                    |   |
	| Product Field and Value | sizing                   | 1 |
	| Product Field and Value | licenses                 | 1 |
	| Product Field and Value | version                  | 7 |
	| Quantity                | 1                        |   |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       |   |
	| Status                  | Approved                 |   |
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Osbzen - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "Platinum Subscription" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | false                    | |
	| Quantity                | 1                        | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                 | |
	And I synchronize the account entitlement definition with the name "Platinum Subscription"
	# Necessary pause for tags and zendesk org sync. Analyze if can be taken out or reduced once account index improves
	And I wait for "1" minutes
	Then the support organization with the code "OSBZENOSBZEN" should be part of the support site
